SCENARIO 08 - MQRC 2035 AUTHORIZATION FAILURE
Executed: 2026-05-10T21:13:54+08:00
Purpose: Demonstrate IBM MQ authorization failure handling without changing the real application credentials.

Simulation method:
- Started a temporary pod: recon-mqrc2035-simulator
- Used the real producer container image: 860510876120.dkr.ecr.ap-southeast-1.amazonaws.com/recon-producer-app:2c91e30b8171
- Disabled AWS Secrets Manager for that temporary pod only: AWS_SECRETS_ENABLED=false
- Injected an intentionally wrong MQ password: MQ_PASSWORD=wrong-password-for-mqrc2035
- Targeted real IBM MQ service: ibm-mq.recon-platform.svc.cluster.local(1414)

Expected failure:
- IBM MQ rejects the client connection because authentication is invalid.
- Application logs classify the failure as MQRC 2035 / MQRC_NOT_AUTHORIZED.
- Real producer, consumer, dashboard, and IBM MQ remain healthy.

MQRC 2035 proof:
JMSWMQ2013: security authentication was not valid for queue manager QM1; IBM MQ reason 2035 MQRC_NOT_AUTHORIZED.
